      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "#2 sounds like https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1181-grabbing-is-animated-physics-bones-stutters-doesnt-actually-move . I don't know that this post should be merged into the one i linked, simply because this post also covers other issues.\n#3 makes #2 worse than it already is. I just did some digging, there's a field VRCPhysBoneBase.configHasUpdated which causes the script to respond to changes in the parameters. It's set to true when modifying stuff in the inspector, and I guess it isn't set to true when an animation sets values on the script. I threw together a quick script to set configHasUpdated to true, and the changes an animation might make (or at the very least the isAnimated toggle, which is what I tested) are indeed handled when that field is set.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
